      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors Impacting Utah Roof Pricing"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-off and Disposal: Removing multiple layers of old shingles adds to labor and dump fees."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Pitch and Complexity: Steep slopes, multiple stories, dormers, and valleys require extra safety equipment and labor."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Wind and Weather Ratings: Many Northern Utah and canyon-adjacent areas require high-wind-rated shingles (such as 130 MPH systems) to withstand severe gusts.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Permits and Warranties: Local building permits usually add up to $500, while extended manufacturer or workmanship warranties can range from $500 to $5,000.",
